  "notes": "{間違|まちが}う is an intransitive verb meaning to be wrong or make a mistake.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Related: {間違|まちが}える (transitive, to mistake one thing for another)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {道|みち}を{間違|まちが}う (take the wrong road)\n- {答|こた}えを{間違|まちが}う (get the answer wrong)\n- {間違|まちが}っている (is wrong/incorrect)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {間違|まちが}い: mistake, error (noun)\n- {間違|まちが}いない: no mistake, definitely",
